PACKAGE MANAGEMENT COMMANDS
**********************************************
1. For installing the package

   Command : yum install package -y

# Example:

yum install git -y

2. For removing the package

Command: yum remove package -y

# Example:

yum remove httpd -y

3. For update the package

Command : yum update -y

# Example:

yum update -y

4.For search the package

Command : yum search package

# Example:

yum search nginx

5. For information about the package

Command : yum info package

# Example:

yum info docker

6. To check installed packages

Command : yum list installed

# Example:

yum list installed

7.To check updates

Command : yum check-update

# Example:

yum check-update

8.To clear cache

Command : yum clean all

# Example:

yum clean all

9.To reinstall package

Command :yum reinstall package -y

# Example:

yum reinstall git -y

10.To list available packages

Command : yum list available

# Example:

yum list available

11.Show dependencies

Command : yum deplist package

# Example:

yum deplist httpd

12.Install specific version

Command : yum install package-version

# Example:

yum install httpd-2.4.37 -y

13.Transaction history

 Command : yum history

# Example:

Command : yum history

14.Undo transaction

Command : yum history undo <id>

# Example:

yum history undo 5

15.Redo transaction

Command : yum history redo <id>

# Example:

yum history redo 5

16.Transaction details

Command : yum history info <id>

# Example:

yum history info 5


*REPOSITORY MANAGEMENT
***********************************

17. List enabled repos

Command : yum repolist

# Example:

yum repolist

18.List all repos

Command : yum repolist all

# Example:

yum repolist all

19.Enable repo

Command : yum config-manager --set-enabled repo-name

# Example:

yum config-manager --set-enabled AppStream

20.Disable repo

Command : yum config-manager --set-disabled repo-name

# Example:

yum config-manager --set-disabled AppStream

21.Repo info

Command : yum repoinfo

# Example:

yum repoinfo

22.Disabled repos

Command : yum repolist disabled

# Example:

yum repolist disabled

23.Install from repo

Command : yum install package --enablerepo=repo-name

# Example:

yum install nginx --enablerepo=epel -y

24.Disable repo temporarily

Command : yum install package --disablerepo=repo-name

# Example:


yum install nginx --disablerepo=epel



GROUP MANAGEMENT COMMANDS
*********************************************

25.List groups

Command : yum group list

# Example:

yum group list

26.Installed groups

Command : yum group list installed

# Example:

yum group list installed

27.Available groups

Command : yum group list available

# Example:

yum group list available

28.Install group

Command : yum groupinstall "Group Name" -y

# Example:

yum groupinstall "Development Tools" -y

29.Remove group

Command : yum groupremove "Group Name" -y

# Example:

yum groupremove "Development Tools" -y

30.Group info

Command : yum group info "group-name"

# Example:

yum group info "Development Tools"

31.Update group

Command : yum group update "group-name"

# Example:

yum group update "Development Tools"